1":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0}},"autoHeightenLevel":{"value":null}},"_id":"zjGhzrrSxKh0jXwX","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/spellcastingEntry.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"spell","name":"Black Hole","folder":"n9rlYzcYkS2bCnVO","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You tear a minuscule hole in the fabric of reality, opening up a pinpoint portal that connects to the outskirts of a black hole deep in the void between worlds. Creatures and unattended objects in the area take 14d6 bludgeoning damage and are drawn toward the portal at the center of the area based on the results of their Fortitude save. If the spell would pull a creature or an object with at least 5 Bulk into an occupied space, the target is instead relocated to the nearest unoccupied square to its destination.</p><p>Dead or destroyed creatures and destroyed objects are not protected from entering and passing through occupied spaces; if they enter the portal's space, they are pulled through into the black hole and annihilated, and this movement through the portal has the teleportation trait.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature or object is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature or object takes half damage and is pulled up to 5 feet toward the portal.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature or object takes full damage and is pulled up to 20 feet toward the portal.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature or object takes double damage and is pulled into the portal's space.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 2d6.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"